From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 02:40:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(kanban): cache attention counts per origin scope and
 share done-check verdicts [daveey]

/api/profiles/projects/tree annotates every profile in one request. attention_task_counts kept a
single-slot cache, so each profile evicted the previous one and the 30 s TTL never hit: every tree
poll (Desktop, every 10 s) re-ran every registered done check for every profile (48 board reads on
the hub, 1.1 s isolated, 2-2.5 s in the live backend under load) and evicted the default profile,
whose next /api/sessions/<id> re-ran them too (5.05 s -> Desktop 5 s timeout, 10-29 18:42 PDT).

Now the counts are cached per scope (bounded at 64 scopes, in kanban_session_activity_attention.py), and a done check's verdict is memoised
for the same TTL by (visible boards, board, card id, completed_at, title, summary), so profiles on
one kanban root share it. Measured on the hub's real boards: tree 1.1 s -> 0.1 s, default annotate
after a tree 0.19 s -> 0.007 s, zero attention board reads on a warm poll.
